.         /*To test this hypothesis, I will use variable plh0303, which ask res
> pondents whether men should be involved in housework, as the dependent variab
> le. This is a four-point ordinal variable ranging from `agree completely' to 
> `disagree completely. The variable would be coded so higher values reflect hi
> gher support. The data will be analyzed with generalized linear model, specif
> ically with ordinal    logit. This allows the model to better reflect the str
> ucture of the dependent variable. The only predictor in the regression would 
> be having a daughter. Since the treatment is randomly assigned, I do not fore
> see any potential for confounding. While other variables may affect values of
>  the dependent variable, they will not affect the values of the independent v
> ariable (given the selection on having children). This precludes the need for
>  additional controls or the incorporation of any clustering structure in the 
> data.  */ 
